Scaling: SDD

Purpose:
  Define scaling rules for all system tiers. Scaling decisions are
  driven by ProjectScale and validated against actual load.

Owns: architecture\scaling.sdd
Principles:
  Scale horizontally before vertically.
  Scale stateless layers before stateful layers.
  Cache before adding more compute.
  Read replicas before sharding.
  Measure before scaling.

VerticalScaling:
  description: Increase capacity of a single node
  when_to_use: L0-L1, temporary spikes
  trigger: CPU > 70%, RAM > 80%, response time degradation
  limit: beyond limits, horizontal is mandatory

HorizontalScaling:
  description: Add more nodes to distribute load
  when_to_use: L2+, stateless services, high traffic
  requirement: application MUST be stateless or externalize state
  trigger: CPU > 60% across nodes, request queue depth growing

AutoScaling:
  description: Automatic scaling based on metrics
  when_to_use: variable traffic, L2+, cloud infrastructure
  metrics: CPU (target 60-70%), request count, queue depth, memory
  policy:
    scale_up_when: metric > threshold for 2 minutes
    scale_down_when: metric < threshold for 5 minutes
    cooldown: 2 minutes
    min_nodes: 2 for HA

DatabaseScaling:
  ReadReplicas:
    description: Replicate primary DB to read-only replicas
    when_to_use: read-heavy (read:write > 10:1), L2+
    routing: writes -> primary, reads -> replica pool
    trigger: primary CPU > 70%, read latency p95 > target

  Sharding:
    description: Partition data across multiple database instances
    when_to_use: data volume exceeds single node, L3+
    rule: MUST optimize queries, add replicas, partition before sharding

  Partitioning:
    description: Split table data within a single database
    when_to_use: large tables (100M+ rows), time-series, multi-tenant
    strategies: range, hash, list

CacheScaling:
  description: Scale caching layers to reduce DB load
  layers: CDN, reverse proxy cache, application cache, distributed cache
  trigger: cache hit rate < 90%, memory > 80%

QueueScaling:
  description: Scale message queues for async processing
  when_to_use: async workflows, event-driven, L2+
  trigger: consumer lag increasing, queue depth growing

LoadBalancing:
  description: Distribute traffic across healthy nodes
  types: L4 (TCP/UDP), L7 (HTTP/HTTPS)
  algorithms: round-robin, least-connections, weighted, ip-hash
  health_checks: active periodic probe, passive error monitoring

AntiPatterns:
  PrematureScaling: MUST measure for at least one full load cycle
  VerticalOnly: horizontal scaling MUST be planned before vertical limits
  Overprovisioning: scale to measured needs with 20% headroom
  Underprovisioning: capacity planning MUST include growth projection
  ScalingWithoutMonitoring: all scaling decisions MUST be metric-driven
  ShardingTooEarly: MUST optimize before sharding
  IgnoringState: identify and scale the slowest tier first
  SingleAZ: production MUST span multiple AZs for HA

Navigation:
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd

State: +
